course: dictionary
lesson: 14491
title: Payable and money words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Payable is an adjective. It describes something that must be paid, or can be paid, often by a certain time. Look at the words around it for clues. «The fee is payable in advance.» The words in advance mean before, so payable here means it must be paid before the thing starts.
explain: «The bill is payable by Friday.» The clue is by Friday, a deadline. The money must be paid by then. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try "to be paid" in the sentence instead of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Money words often come in set phrases. Payable monthly means paid each month, and amount payable means the total you have to pay. In maths, the amount payable is the price left to pay after a discount or with tax added.
fact: Payable is an adjective: it describes a bill, a fee, a cheque or an amount.
fact: Payable means must be paid, or can be paid, often by a certain time.
fact: A cheque payable to someone is one that will be paid to that person.
fact: «Payable in advance» means paid before you receive something.
fact: «Amount payable» means the total you have to pay, for example after a discount.
exercise: «The fee is payable in advance.» What does payable mean here? | *Must be paid, before the thing starts | Very heavy | Lost forever | Given away for free
exercise: A cheque payable to Mia will be paid to whom? | The shop next door | *Mia | The cheque itself | The bank manager
exercise: In maths, the amount payable is the total after a discount. Which word is closest in meaning to payable? | Broken | Painted | Hidden | *Due to be paid
test: «The rent is payable monthly.» How often must the rent be paid? | Every hour | *Each month | Never | Once a year
test: Which phrase means the money must be paid first, before anything else happens? | Payable monthly | Payable to Sam | Amount payable | *Payable in advance
exam: Ben sees «Tickets payable by Friday» on a sign. What must he do? | *Pay for the tickets by Friday | Sell the sign to the shop | Give the tickets back | Lose the tickets on Friday
